                                "example_id": "5b4e93fc-4471-43a6-a9db-ed5f3c073ab0",
                                "sense_id": "3a4bbcad-d04a-3c7e-ac35-9c09af484915",
                                "text": "Na plac budowy przywieziono elementy konstrukcyjne dźwigu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ab0955c-1a54-43d1-a029-a5f82b1dabb5",
                                "sense_id": "3a4bbcad-d04a-3c7e-ac35-9c09af484915",
                                "text": "Jeszcze rozsądniej, ciekawiej od strony konstrukcyjnej, zabezpieczono zespół napędowy przed emisją nadmiaru podczerwieni."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7eb97868-1d6a-4a63-92a1-b5e0ceb6156b",
                        "source_entry_id": "33257f9b-82f4-3493-9e43-6557af75cdff",
                        "source_sense_id": "3a4bbcad-d04a-3c7e-ac35-9c09af484915",
                        "target_lang_word": "structural",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "structural",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0755e384-b80a-3e2d-8507-1cef03626180",
                                        "entry_id": "89a6634d-cf56-3462-8ffd-a2d2b0a71c43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or having structure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51bc2629-ff1b-40f0-8150-3aa0dbf64ab1",
                                                "sense_id": "0755e384-b80a-3e2d-8507-1cef03626180",
                                                "text": "Class 1. consists of nervous diseases, such as depend on the nervous and muscular systems; the second, of sanguine diseases, such as depend on the sanguiferous system; the third, of secretory diseases, or such as are connected with the state of the secretions; and the fourth, of structural diseases, or those that are connected with the nutritive powers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f94433c5-af4d-45f9-9435-40505bbf20c7",
                                                "sense_id": "0755e384-b80a-3e2d-8507-1cef03626180",
                                                "text": "These structural differences, the authors suggest, support previous reports of differences in personality: liberals tend to be better at managing conflicting information, while conservatives are though to be better at recognizing threats, researchers said."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2fac459e-6eae-3eb0-b770-bd26d0773afe",
                                        "entry_id": "89a6634d-cf56-3462-8ffd-a2d2b0a71c43",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Involving the mechanics of construction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "structural",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c0588ed-0165-3efb-bf47-09292dd9de06",
                                        "entry_id": "f0097247-45aa-3cdd-aa7f-6db6cc605557",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Structural steel, used in construction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a934f697-2767-466d-9587-9580ad267761",
                                                "sense_id": "2c0588ed-0165-3efb-bf47-09292dd9de06",
                                                "text": "Freight differentials often increased the spread in favor of the imported structurals. Purchasers repeatedly emphasized that their purchases of imported structurals were split among a number of sources, including Spain, France, West Germany, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b94c9280-d668-4878-830f-c5c0cb686496",
                        "source_entry_id": "33257f9b-82f4-3493-9e43-6557af75cdff",
                        "source_sense_id": "3a4bbcad-d04a-3c7e-ac35-9c09af484915",
                        "target_lang_word": "constructional",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "constructional",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                        "entry_id": "ddde7b1f-3d9a-3c47-a3a0-2b6436cc54b1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, pertaining to, or obtained by construction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab4332b5-f7da-4973-8bb1-67ff3386e711",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "What mortal conception of constructional power and grace can equal the gothic cathedral of the middle age, in which we see a proportion and a delicacy . . ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c614572-2da8-4ce1-85ff-e5f6ae4d2ab0",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "1869 The Universal Decorator\nNo other constructional features projecting from the walls occur in any of these buildings, with the single exception of buttresses"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1effee06-0567-4888-9a92-314f1273ae45",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "To keep constructional costs to a minimum track formations were narrower than is now customary, many tunnels were unlined, timber was largely used for bridging, and 85 lb. per yd. rails were regarded as adequate."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7367f14e-9e70-47a8-8af1-1e20b402301c",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "The bodywork employs, where possible, the same constructional methods as for the standard B.R. coaching stock, in order to utilise existing jigs and press tools."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1e5b117-6a5c-4548-9905-b6099f5a3cb1",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "After some quite speedy constructional work the line was opened to traffic on January 2, 1865."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3df05043-a6fc-4757-9a1c-64901f2f0095",
                                                "sense_id": "29f3008f-661a-3798-aa8a-1160cb238a9b",
                                                "text": "Between 1820 and 1849, wooden toys were made in Pennsylvania by Asa Crandall, the father of Charles M. Crandall who made games, picture blocks and puzzles such as 'Pigs in Clover'. It was Charles M. Crandall who made the constructional game of acrobats, ,the limbs fitting together with grooves and the parts painted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
